WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.830
(upbeat music)

2
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.300
There's no place like home.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.990
And that's why we're celebrating

4
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.220
as many hometowns as we can.

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.100
All across the country, all season long.

6
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.710
Next up is Portland, Oregon

7
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:18.440
where culinary professional, Judiaann Woo calls home.

8
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.090
I hear she makes it her mission

9
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.600
to know all the best restaurants and chefs in town.

10
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.440
Now that's a woman after my own heart.

11
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.273
Let's watch.

12
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.220 line:15%
Hey, Drew, it is Kara Mack,

13
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.100 line:15%
host of KATU's "Afternoon Live",

14
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.120 line:15%
your sibling show in Portland, Oregon

15
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.630
and I know you're celebrating hometown spirit.

16
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.780
Well, no one has more hometown spirit

17
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.870 line:15%
than our very own Judiaann Woo.

18
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.450 line:15%
Judiaann, share with people why Portland's so awesome.

19
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.700
Portland is my hometown and I love it so much.

20
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.200
There were so many amazing places to eat and drink.

21
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.730
Plus scenic beauty and the most passionate

22
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.500
and creative people you will ever meet.

23
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.130
And you're gonna show it off for everyone.

24
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.942
So we're gonna send you off, have so much fun.

25
00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:56.690 line:15%
(upbeat music)

26
00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.100
Welcome to OMSI.

27
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.680
OMSI stands for the Oregon Museum of Science and Industry.

28
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.210
It's got something for everybody.

29
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.050
You learn about the earth, the universe,

30
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.660
and everything in between.

31
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.090 line:15%
We have here giant Australian walking sticks.

32
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.100 line:15%
This is one corner of the museum

33
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.010 line:15%
where they have actual live creatures

34
00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.900 line:15%
that you can interact with such as these.

35
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.253
Say hello to Drew.

36
00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.950
I'm here at Toki restaurant

37
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.740
in the heart of downtown Portland

38
00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.780
and behind me is chef-owner, Peter Cho.

39
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.170 line:15%
He's doing his take on the most delicious,

40
00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:32.070 line:15%
crave-worthy Korean American classics.

41
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.970 line:15%
This is like, you know, portable food.

42
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.523 line:15%
So good.
Yes.

43
00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.040
Portland is also known as The Rose City

44
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.030
and what better place to wrap up our tour

45
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:46.010
than the International Rose Test Gardens.

46
00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:46.900 line:15%
Here on the grounds,

47
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.570 line:15%
we have 10,000 different bushes representing

48
00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:52.030 line:15%
over 610 varieties of roses

49
00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:54.620
in every single color imaginable.

50
00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.990
It's the ultimate place to find your zen.

51
00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.650
Well Drew, that was just a quick peek at Portland,

52
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.510
the city we love so much.

53
00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.480
We can't wait for you to come visit.

54
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.323
See ya soon.

55
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.650
Thanks, Judiaann.

56
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:11.140
I remember going to Naomi Pomeroy's restaurant, Beast,

57
00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.140
and we hung out all night long.

58
00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.950
One of the great nights of my life.

59
00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:18.270
We're definitely hanging out the next time I'm in Portland.

60
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.136
See you soon.

61
00:02:19.136 --> 00:02:21.719 line:15%
(upbeat music)

